{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1137150-what-is-the-cost-of-maxing-out-everything","id":1137150,"title":"What is the cost of Maxing Out everything?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-03T18:41:38-07:00","id":1137150,"title":"What is the cost of Maxing Out everything?","content":"So simple question, but with a potentially complicated answer. How much exp is neccesary for a member of a specific splat to buy everything in their core rulebooks under the following rules:<br /> <br /> <br /> -Start with typical member of a given splat follosing standard generation rules.<br /> -No experience cost reductions are in effect.<br /> -Purchase base attributes and skills up to 10.<br /> -If possible max out Power Stats, Integrity, and magical traits up to 10 or 5 if able.<br /> -Purchase all merits and supernatural powers in the splatbook. The core bluebook rulesbook doesnt exist as far as we are concerned. If powers are subsplat specific such as the way Auspice gifts are, go for the most expensive path possible that a single character can legally have. (As a bonus, i do actually wonder how things would be to also include mutually exclusive picks)<br /> -Selections that may be chosen multiple times (such as a Demons Cover) are selected once, or if a trait purchase lists it as a prerequisite, as many times as necceaary to meet those requirements.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, how much is stuff really worth?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T19:29:10-07:00","id":1137161,"title":"","content":"You're talking 2e or 1e? Everything is flat-cost in 2e, so the exercise basically is down to multiplying all the blank dots in a sheet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T21:45:28-07:00","id":1137190,"title":"","content":"Assuming 2nd Edition and core books only?<br /> <br /> <b>Blue Book:</b> 586 (96 for all Attributes to 5, 196 for all Skills to 5, 6 for Integrity to 10, and 296 for all Merits to their maximum [assuming we're including Esoteric Armory and assuming you allow a character with Alternate Identity to take Fame on one identity and Anonymity on the other].)<br /> <br /> <b>Requiem: </b>1198- (272 for all Attributes to 10, 436 for all Skills to 10, 173 for all Merits to their maximum [assuming the character is any clan other than Ventrue, which is the only Clan without a 1-dot Clan-specific Merit, assuming the character identifies as female so they can take Undead Menses, and assuming you allow a character with Alternate Identity to take Fame on one identity and Anonymity on the other], 6 for Humanity to 10, 45 for Blood Potency to 10, 45 for 3 In-Clan Disciplines to 5 [assuming all three free Disciplines went into in-Clan], 200 for 8 Out-of-Clan Disciplines to 5, 66 for all Devotions.)<br /> <i> Carthian Movement:</i> 29 (29 for all Clan-specific Merits [assuming you take 5 dots of Covenant Status in non-Carthian Covenants using Right of Return].)<br /> <i>Circle of the Crone:</i> 39 (20 for Cruac to 5, 10 for all Cruac Rites, 9 for all Clan-specific Merits.)<br /> <i>Invictus:</i> 15 (15 for all Clan-specific Merits)<br /> <i>Lancea et Sanctum:</i> 36 (20 for Theban Sorcery to 5, 8 for all Theban Sorcery Miracles, 8 for all Clan-specific Merits)<br /> <i> Ordo Dracul: 97 </i>(20 for 1 In-Mystery Coil to 5, 50 for 2 Out-Of-Mystery Coils, 20 for all Scales [assuming all are bought without the prerequisite Coil], 7 for all Clan-specific Merits)<br /> <br /> The maximum possible cost is 1390 (assuming Carthian Status 5 and all other Covenant Status 1 using Right of Return, allows for all advantages from all Covenants, -4 dots of Merits that require Invictus Status &gt; 1)<br /> <br /> That took me much longer than I thought it would, so I'm taking a break before I do this with any more lines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-04-2017, 10:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T01:21:33-07:00","id":1137236,"title":"","content":"Awesome your great at this please do micro templates if you can","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T02:28:59-07:00","id":1137248,"title":"","content":"Ok, so I did Mage, which is a little tricky because they have merits like Artifact and Imbued item that can be taken multiple times and have variable ratings, and also a lot of their merits preclude each other.<br /> <br /> So my final tally was 1800<i>ish. </i>That's every arcarnum maxed,. every spell in the book taken as both a rote and a praxis, a legacy, max wisdom, and 126 dots of merits. Including both mentor and infamous mentor, which don't really make a lot of sense for a tenth degree master.<br /> <br /> I guess you could also take an imbued item and an artifact for every spell as well, which could easily push it over 3000.<br /> <br /> Oh, also you could take enough grimoires to cover every spell. That's an extra 144 experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 09-04-2017, 05:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T05:52:05-07:00","id":1137268,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> I'm confused by the requiem part about getting integrity to ten. Are we speaking about ghouls in this case? If memory serves vampires don't have integrity, only humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T07:09:15-07:00","id":1137284,"title":"","content":"Integrity and humanity are, for the purposes of this exercise, the same damn thing. <br /> <br /> Although I think mortal integrity actually costs 3 exp per dot so taking it to 10 would cost 9, not 6.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T07:43:49-07:00","id":1137294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1137150-what-is-the-cost-of-maxing-out-everything?p=1137268#post1137268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> I'm confused by the requiem part about getting integrity to ten. Are we speaking about ghouls in this case? If memory serves vampires don't have integrity, only humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just a typo, it should say Humanity to 10.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1137150-what-is-the-cost-of-maxing-out-everything?p=1137284#post1137284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although I think mortal integrity actually costs 3 exp per dot so taking it to 10 would cost 9, not 6.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to the chart on page 77 of Chronicles, it costs 2.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1137150-what-is-the-cost-of-maxing-out-everything?p=1137248#post1137248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so I did Mage, which is a little tricky because they have merits like Artifact and Imbued item that can be taken multiple times and have variable ratings, and also a lot of their merits preclude each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>These situations are accounted for in the instructions - of a feature can be taken multiple times, take it only once, and if features are exclusive, take the more expensive feature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-04-2017, 10:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T07:55:54-07:00","id":1137304,"title":"","content":"Yeah but technically there's no upper limit on the dot cost of an artifact. You could, theoretically, build one capable of casting every spell in the book that costs a few hundred dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T08:24:21-07:00","id":1137316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1137150-what-is-the-cost-of-maxing-out-everything?p=1137304#post1137304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah but technically there's no upper limit on the dot cost of an artifact. You could, theoretically, build one capable of casting every spell in the book that costs a few hundred dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, yeah, looking at Artifact... You could have a single Artifact with the effect of every spell in the book, each with all 10 Utility attainments applied to it. That would be half the total number of dots of every spell in the book, plus 10x the number of spells in the book, plus 2 since the single most powerful effect doesn't have its Arcanum cost cut in half.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T09:22:59-07:00","id":1137333,"title":"","content":"That does raise the question of if an artifact's effective gnosis can go over ten.<br /> <br /> If so, I wouldn't like to meet the guy wielding the Omnisphere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T09:29:56-07:00","id":1137335,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://vignette3.wikia.nocookie.net/assassinscreed/images/5/5f/Apple_Retrieval_8.png/revision/latest?cb=20121016154741\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T12:04:36-07:00","id":1137392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1137150-what-is-the-cost-of-maxing-out-everything#post1137150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, how much is stuff really worth?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was starting with Werewolf but became curious what the point was. Werewolves get a lot of free stuff. Attributes through Merits, Gifts through Renown, Skills through Tribe. So without the cost decreases, there seems little relevancy to how much things cost, as it's not a cost that would ever be associated with gameplay, and one might as well be asking how many vowels there are in the book.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T14:58:59-07:00","id":1137459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1137150-what-is-the-cost-of-maxing-out-everything?p=1137392#post1137392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was starting with Werewolf but became curious what the point was. Werewolves get a lot of free stuff. Attributes through Merits, Gifts through Renown, Skills through Tribe. So without the cost decreases, there seems little relevancy to how much things cost, as it's not a cost that would ever be associated with gameplay, and one might as well be asking how many vowels there are in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the note about cost decreases was for things like Professional Training so it doesn't mess with the cost depending on the order you buy stuff in. If I do it for werewolf, I'd assume the character takes Wolf Gifts with his free Facets whenever possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T15:23:04-07:00","id":1137471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1137150-what-is-the-cost-of-maxing-out-everything?p=1137459#post1137459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the note about cost decreases was for things like Professional Training so it doesn't mess with the cost depending on the order you buy stuff in. If I do it for werewolf, I'd assume the character takes Wolf Gifts with his free Facets whenever possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>What did you do for Specialties? Skip them or one per Skill?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T15:34:15-07:00","id":1137478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbc