eg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T16:15:47-07:00","id":1137499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1137150-what-is-the-cost-of-maxing-out-everything?p=1137481#post1137481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you count In-Clan Disciplines as a cost reduction?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, cause there's no way to buy them for 5 experiences. 4 experiences isn't a reduction, it's just what they cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T17:06:51-07:00","id":1137509,"title":"","content":"Okay, Almarck said to go the most expensive route. So rather than using the 'free' Gifts on Wolf Gifts, I decided the werewolf got every Shadow Gift in the core, then got his Renown, except for 1 dot in each non-character creation one, since he needs Renown in something to be able to get a Gift according to it. I picked a Cahalith Blood Talon, because it was the first option for Auspice and Tribe. Fortunately they had an overlapping Affinity Gift, Inspiration, so they got the whole Gift set for free to prepare the rest for really expensive stuff. Each tribe has a Merit, but they're all 2 dots. Each tribe has a rite at varying dot levels but the Blood Talon one is only 2 Dots.<br /> <br /> Obviously you're meant to create more Shadow Gifts on your own, we have one in the Giver of Gifts blog, but for a while any Gifts the werewolf got outside of the core would be 'free' due to their saved up Renown 'credit.'<br /> <br /> The end result was 1212 Experiences.<br /> 45 to buy Primal Urge all the way up. 276 for all the Attributes, 434 for all the Skills, 150 for all the Merits. 66 for the Renown. 9 Experience to break into his other Affinity Gifts, 55 to break into all the other Non-Affinity Gifts, 112 for all Facets, 15 for all Wolf Gifts. And 50 for the Rites.<br /> <br /> Give me a bit and I'll go through a suitably disadvantaged Ghost Wolf that doesn't meddle Renown.<br /> <br /> Ghost Wolves only get two Affinity Gifts, but if you take advantage of all the free Gifts from Renown and count out Tribe-only rites and Merits the cost is 1168 Experiences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-04-2017, 08:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}